ng technical, responsibility, concentration, problem solving, but hot temper could be a safety risk under pressure. However D responds to unexpected events adequately, which suggests some stress resilience. Hot temper may manifest under stress. Not sure.\n\nB has strong stress handling, conscientious, but communication issue nasty remarks could affect crew. Memory weakness for numbers could affect attention.\n\nA has strong anticipation, leadership, but show-off and not open to new ideas may affect crew cooperation and adaptability.\n\nC has quick correct decisions, calm, technical, but egocentric, communication difficulty, unwilling to further education.\n\nOverall, perhaps Candidate D balances strengths across many criteria, with only hot temper as concern. But hot temper could be severe. However D also takes responsibility seriously, concentrates, solves problems, responds adequately to unexpected events. That seems strong.\n\nCandidate B also strong but communication issue nasty remarks may be more severe than hot temper? Both are serious.\n\nWe need to pick one. I think D is best overall, as strengths cover many criteria, and the hot temper may be mitigated by responsibility and concentration. So I will recommend Candidate D.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the current set of facts...\". Provide evidence: D concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, responds adequately to unexpected events. Concern: hot temper, know-it-all. Explain why still best.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate D\"."}
