The egocentric and communication difficulty could affect crew cooperation and professional communication. But positive crew atmosphere suggests good cooperation. The egocentric may be mitigated.\n\nD strengths: concentration, problem solving, responsibility, adequate response. Concerns: hot temper, know-it-all, weak leadership, moody, loner. Those are serious for crew cooperation and communication.\n\nThus C seems stronger overall. Emily may change vote to C, citing evidence. She should reference James and Sarah's points, and explain why C's reliability and crew atmosphere outweigh D's concerns. She can also note that D's hot temper and weak leadership are more severe than C's communication issues.\n\nThus produce public message: \"I agree with James and Sarah that C's reliability and crew atmosphere outweigh D's strengths, so I shift my recommendation to Candidate C.\" Provide evidence: C 100% reliability, positive crew atmosphere, quick correct decisions; D hot temper, weak leadership, know-it-all.\n\nNow produce metadata JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
